librist source pin
==================

`./src` is **pristine upstream librist** at:

    commit 6377b5c333a404e3bd7db789f1ba880d9abba07e
    "Merge branch 'feature/prometheus-avg-buffer-time' into 'master'"
    repo https://code.videolan.org/rist/librist.git

It is the second parent of the merge commit (`813e68c`) in the fork
`patricecarter`/`patcarter883`'s librist fork — i.e. the exact upstream tree the fork was
based on. `src/` carries no `.git`: it is a plain vendored tree so it can be tracked by this
repository.

Every open-broadcast change is a patch in this directory, applied to the copy in
`$(PKG_BUILD_DIR)` by `Build/Prepare` (`$(Build/Patch)`, `PATCH_DIR` defaults to `./patches`):

| patch | scope |
|---|---|
| `001-librist-receiver-fixes.patch` | Two upstream-quality librist bug fixes (not product-specific — worth upstreaming): **`src/rist-common.c`** replaces `assert(packet_time < next->packet_time)` in the retry-interpolation path with a clamp to preserve strict ordering (a VBR source, or a neighbour mismatch across a seq wrap, makes the CBR estimate land at/after the next packet time and used to SIGABRT the process); it also fixes `rist_peer_recv_wrap` so the receive loop runs at least once on Windows. **`src/udp.c`** stops double-counting data bandwidth — `rist_calculate_bitrate()` was called in the RTCP path *and* by its callers. |
| `002-rist2rist-wan-telemetry.patch` | The open-broadcast feature and its hardening: the `rist2rist` proxy emits its **WAN-leg** link quality back to the encoder over **RIST OOB** (new `RIST_OOB_API_IP_IDENT_TELEMETRY` = 54322, `tools/oob_shared.[ch]` + `tools/rist2rist.c`) so the encoder drives adaptive bitrate through the bridge exactly as it does against a direct receiver. Includes this session's reliability fixes: a telemetry mutex (librist runs a separate sender and receiver protocol thread per context, so the telemetry globals *were* raced), SIGTERM handling (procd stops with SIGTERM; the `out:` cleanup never used to run), the hot-path `assert` replaced by a NULL check, the master relay loop's `ret < 0` backoff branch, and the stats-JSON dump moved INFO → DEBUG. |

Regenerating
------------

Only the patches named in `series` are applied — that is why this README is safe sitting here.
Add a new patch to BOTH this directory and `series`, or it will be silently ignored.

Do **not** edit `./src` and commit the result — that reintroduces the untracked embedded-repo
problem this layout exists to fix. Edit a scratch copy of librist, then regenerate:

    git -C <librist checkout> diff <base-commit> -- <files> > patches/00N-....patch

Verify a patch still applies and reproduces the intended tree before committing it:

    patch -p1 --dry-run -d <pristine copy> < patches/00N-....patch
